    question: 'How does UAE handle digital divorce for non-Muslims?',
    answer: 'Non-Muslims in UAE are governed by Federal Decree-Law No. 41 of 2022 (civil personal status law). Under this law, there is no talaq and therefore no digital divorce mechanism. WhatsApp messages from one spouse to another saying "I want a divorce" are not a divorce, they are just communication. Non-Muslims must file for civil no-fault dissolution at the Personal Status Court. The message itself has no legal consequence for the marital status, though it could be used as evidence of the intention to divorce in proceedings.',
